    ('Hotel neon sign', 'Look for grand illuminated letters above older hotel entrances, often with flowing cursive designs that glow in warm pinks, blues, or reds against the night sky.', 'Identify a neon sign displaying ''HOTEL'' text in glowing tubes. The sign must show the full word clearly with characteristic neon tubing and a lit appearance against a dark background.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Neon signs don''t produce heat, making them ideal for hotels—they can run continuously without raising cooling costs or creating fire hazards.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/687f4ed07ad9b50d.png', 0),
    ('Motel arrow sign', 'Find the classic pointing arrow signs with neon tubes that light up directionally, usually mounted on tall poles outside 1950s-60s motels along highways.', 'Locate a neon arrow pointing directionally alongside or above ''MOTEL'' text. The arrow must be formed from neon tubes, illuminated and pointing left, right, up, or down.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Glowing arrow signs are so iconic to motels that many are now protected as historical landmarks, despite once being considered eyesores.', null, 1),
    ('Diner neon lettering', 'Search for bright neon letters spelling out diner names or ''EATS'' on the storefront, typically red or blue tubes forming bold, recognizable typography.', 'Find neon tubes spelling ''DINER'' or diner-related words. The lettering must be glowing neon, clearly legible, and mounted on or part of a diner establishment''s exterior.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Neon''s warm glow was chosen for diners specifically because it made food appear more appetizing than the harsh light of incandescent bulbs.', null, 2),
    ('Vintage bar neon', 'Hunt for beer brand names and bar signs glowing in windows, often featuring script lettering or brand logos in classic neon colors like deep red or turquoise.', 'Spot neon signage displaying ''BAR'' or bar-related text in glowing tubes on a building facade. The sign must show characteristic vintage neon styling with illuminated tubes.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Neon tubes were often filled with argon or krypton gas, and breweries paid sign makers extra for rare neon colors that required expensive gases.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/5539b9e0104ffc8f.jpg', 3),
    ('Theater marquee neon', 'Photograph the illuminated movie title displays and border lights framing theater marquees, capturing the bright glow of classic theater signage.', 'Capture a theater marquee with neon lighting around the frame or lettering. The sign must show ''THEATER'', ''CINEMA'', or similar text in neon tubes above an entrance.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Theater marquees using neon tubes became status symbols in the 1930s-40s; theaters competed by installing increasingly elaborate multi-color displays.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/064c12597f52fda4.jpg', 4),
    ('Gasoline station sign', 'Look for old gas pump signs and station branding in neon, often with brand logos like Shell or Texaco glowing above vintage pump islands.', 'Identify vintage neon signage at a gas station displaying brand names like ''SHELL'', ''CHEVRON'', ''TEXACO'', or ''GAS''. The neon tubes must form recognizable lettering or logos.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Gas station neon signs were designed to glow from hundreds of feet away, as customers needed to spot them while driving at night before streetlights became common.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/c9a4579520b1af2e.svg', 5),
    ('Barber shop pole neon', 'Find the rotating red-white-blue poles outside barber shops, and capture any complementary neon ''BARBER'' signs glowing alongside them.', 'Show a neon sign display with ''BARBER'' text or a barber pole design in neon tubes. The characteristic red-white-blue pole or neon lettering must be clearly visible and illuminated.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Some vintage barber shops combined neon with their traditional red-white-blue pole, though most used neon only for shop window signage.', null, 6),
    ('Beauty salon sign', 'Search for neon signs above salons featuring words like ''SALON'' or ''BEAUTY,'' often in soft pinks or purples that reflect in storefront windows.', 'Display a neon sign reading ''BEAUTY SALON'', ''SALON'', or similar beauty-related text in glowing neon tubes. The lettering must be clearly legible on the storefront.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Beauty salons adopted neon signs in the 1920s-30s to advertise permanents and new electric hair treatments, positioning themselves as modern and cutting-edge.', null, 7),
    ('Vintage nightclub sign', 'Look for bold, glamorous neon signs outside clubs with names glowing in bright colors, often with decorative elements like martini glasses or dancing figures.', 'Capture neon signage for a nightclub venue with words like ''CLUB'', ''LOUNGE'', or venue names in glowing neon tubes. The sign must display characteristic vintage nightclub branding.', 'rare'::public.item_rarity, 'Neon signs in nightclubs were technically illegal in some cities during Prohibition (1920-33) unless businesses used codes that owners and patrons understood.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/1e50ebae95ebbcc8.png', 8),
    ('Pawn shop neon', 'Find the ''PAWN'' signs glowing in windows, often surrounded by merchandise displays, typically in yellows, blues, or reds that pierce through dark storefronts.', 'Identify a neon sign displaying ''PAWN'' or ''PAWN SHOP'' in glowing tubes. The lettering must be clearly visible and illuminated in characteristic neon styling.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Pawn shops relied heavily on neon signage because the bright glow signaled that items inside were genuine and worth your attention—a trust-building visual cue.', null, 9),
    ('Vintage laundromat sign', 'Search for illuminated ''LAUNDROMAT'' or ''LAUNDRY'' signs on older self-service laundry buildings, usually in simple block lettering.', 'Show neon lettering spelling ''LAUNDROMAT'' or ''LAUNDRY'' in glowing tubes. The sign must display the full or recognizable text in vintage neon styling on a laundromat storefront.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, '1950s-60s laundromat neon signs were often the only lighting source inside after hours, helping night-shift workers and insomniacs see their machines clearly.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/9dc52db373a2104e.jpg', 10),
    ('Drive-in movie sign', 'Photograph the tall iconic signs marking drive-in theater entrances, with arrows and ''DRIVE-IN'' lettering glowing against the evening sky.', 'Capture neon signage reading ''DRIVE-IN'' or showing a drive-in theater marquee with glowing neon tubes. The sign must clearly indicate a drive-in movie venue.', 'rare'::public.item_rarity, 'Drive-in movie neon marquees had to be readable from moving cars at highway speeds, driving innovation in letter sizing and brightness that influenced all roadside signage.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/d54e06b75a9b9f4d.jpg', 11),
    ('Vintage pharmacy neon', 'Look for pharmacy names and ''RX'' symbols in neon, often with green or white glowing letters on older drugstore storefronts downtown.', 'Display a neon sign reading ''PHARMACY'', ''DRUGS'', or ''RX'' in glowing tubes. The neon lettering must be clearly visible and mounted on a pharmacy storefront.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Pharmacy neon signs often featured plus signs or mortar-and-pestle symbols, creating an early form of visual branding that customers recognized from blocks away.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/5b20498d93e4c8d7.png', 12),
    ('Bowling alley sign', 'Find ''BOWLING'' signs glowing above alleys, often paired with neon bowler silhouettes or pins, typically in bright whites and blues.', 'Identify neon signage displaying ''BOWLING'', ''BOWL'', or ''LANES'' in glowing neon tubes. The lettering must be clearly legible and indicate a bowling establishment.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Bowling alleys embraced neon in the 1940s-50s because the glowing signs matched the excitement of their newly electrified pin-setting machinery inside.', null, 13),
